{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the name of the one was Eliezer, etc.</b> The reason he said <b>the one</b> is that in terms of the reason for the naming, the reason for this one preceded the reason for the name Gershom, for at first He saved him from the sword of Pharaoh, and afterward he came to Midian and sojourned there." "And the reason he did not name Eliezer first is that he named him for the event that had happened to him then, in a foreign land, and only afterward went to seek earlier events. Or according to what we explained in the verse ״גֵּר הָיִיתִי״ (Exodus 2:22), that he intended his sojourning in this world — this dimension preceded his salvation from the sword of Pharaoh, and therefore he placed it first. And in terms of the second dimension of sojourning in a foreign land, there preceded to it the allusion hinted at in the naming of Eliezer; and corresponding to this he said ״the one.״ And for this reason it was necessary to explain what the עֵזֶר (help) was for which he named him, so he said <b>וַיַּצִּלֵנִי</b> (and He delivered me), etc. And through this it is justified to say of it the name <b>the one.</b> And were it not for his saying ״וַיַּצִּלֵנִי מֵחֶרֶב פַּרְעֹה״ (and He delivered me from the sword of Pharaoh), I would have explained that the עֵזֶר was after the sojourning, and the fact that he prefaced by saying ״גֵּר הָיִיתִי״, etc., would have obligated me to explain thus — and the reason for his saying ״the one״ would have been sealed off from my understanding."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:29.061273071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}